* Class A 30 W combo, Normal / Brilliant channels, "AC30 Top Boost" reissue (Vox drawing AC30-60-02, issue 5,
* sheet 1, from drtube.com/schematics/vox/ac30-60-02-iss5.pdf). V8 is one 12AX7 (Brilliant = top triode, Normal =
* bottom triode, shared 1k5 / 22u cathode, 220k plate loads). The Brilliant volume (470k, 470p, 120p bright cap)
* feeds V7a (1k5 / 22u, 100k) and the V7b cathode follower, then the Treble / Bass network; the Normal volume
* (470k, 47n) skips V7 and the tone controls and meets the tone network's output at the 220k / 220k mixer in front
* of the phase inverter (C3, in the power amp netlist). The Vib/Trem channel (V9..V11), its mixing network and the
* footswitch are not modelled.
*
* Reading notes (change these here, not in code):
*  - each channel's two jacks are modelled as the Hi jack: 68k into the grid, 1M leak at the jack node;
*  - the HT feed of V7 (10k + 33u) and V8 (22k + 10u) comes from the amplifier's HT; the drawing prints no
*    voltages, so the rail x is the HT node after the choke.

.nodes x n7 n8 in jn jb gin g8a g8b p8a p8b k8 bt wb nt wn g7 p7a k7 kf ta tb tc tr wt m

* HT (node x): driven from the power amp at run time; 340 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 340
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* HT feeds.
R R56 x n7 10k
C C36 n7 0 33u
R R59 x n8 22k
C C37 n8 0 10u

* Jacks. SW_* select the channel (closed 1 ohm / open 1e12), set by the jack modes.
R SW_N in jn 1
R R29 jn 0 1M
R R31 jn g8b 68k
R SW_B in jb 1e12
R R32 jb 0 1M
R R34 jb g8a 68k

* V8: Brilliant (A) and Normal (B) triodes.
T V8A g8a p8a k8 12AX7
R R57 n8 p8a 220k
T V8B g8b p8b k8 12AX7
R R58 n8 p8b 220k
R R10 k8 0 1k5
C C10 k8 0 22u

* Volume pots (wiper = output); A470k.
C C9 p8a bt 470p
R VR_BT bt wb 1
R VR_BB wb 0 1
C C8 bt wb 120p
C C11 p8b nt 47n
R VR_NT nt wn 1
R VR_NB wn 0 1

* V7a gain stage and V7b cathode follower (grid on V7a's plate).
T V7A wb p7a k7 12AX7
R R55 n7 p7a 100k
R R9 k7 0 1k5
C C7 k7 0 22u
T V7B p7a n7 kf 12AX7
R R8 kf 0 56k

* Treble / Bass network (Top Boost).
R R35 kf ta 100k
C C6 kf tr 47p
C C4 ta tb 22n
C C5 ta tc 22n
R R7 tc 0 10k
R VR_KT tb tc 1
R VR_KB tc 0 1
R VR_TT tr wt 1
R VR_TB wt tb 1

* Mixer in front of the phase inverter: tone stack output (R5) and Normal volume (R6), 220k each.
R R5 wt m 220k
R R6 wn m 220k
